       <narrative xml:lang="EN">In relation to unconditional and unrestricted cash transfers, preparatory and multi-level coordination activities have been carried out to support implementation. Meetings were held with provincial government authorities to present the project and its objectives, followed by district and sector-level engagements where targets was shared by district. In addition, the project was presented in communities assigned by district governments to ensure alignment and understanding at the local level. Furthermore, the vulnerability criteria for the MPCA were disseminated within the communities, promoting awareness and clarity regarding the beneficiary selection process. Additionally a vendor (Vodacom) was identified and registed to be involved on cash transfer. The process of verifying and registering beneficiaries is currently underway in the targeted 6 communities (2 in Xai Xai and 4  in Guija district). Verification and validation activities have been conducted using vulnerability criteria based on beneficiary lists shared by the communities, ensuring transparency and the proper identification of eligible households. Following this process, the registration of beneficiaries who meet the established criteria has begun, ensuring their inclusion in the cash assistance program.</narrative>
