       <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 21 and 22 April 2026, the team carried out a mapping and technical assessment of water points in Nguluzane Zimilene, working alongside SDPI technicians, the Chief of Post Administrative, Village Secretaries and borehole repair technicians. A total of 8 broken boreholes were identified across five communities, Zimilene (2), Nhacumelene (1), Cumbane (1), Mahiyelene (1) and Chilaulene (3) in Xai Xai district. Two boreholes in Zimilene were assessed in detail: one in the 3rd Ward has been non-functional for over a year, while the one in the 4th Ward produces water with visible impurities and drainage failures. It is worth noting that the 4 boreholes originally planned for rehabilitation in Guij&#xe1; District were reassigned to Xai-Xai in Nguluzane, as the district no longer has eligible boreholes. Repair works are scheduled to begin between 27 April and 8 May 2026. No beneficiaries are recorded for this reporting period.</narrative>
